/*
# Lustre

Mobile detailing assistant powered by Gemini. Static PWA (`index.html`, `sw.js`, `manifest.webmanifest`) plus edge functions that keep your API key server-side: `api/chat` (streaming answers), `api/tts` (Gemini voice) and `api/stt` (Cloud “Hey Lustre” listening). All three live in `edge-functions/api/`.

## Deploy
1. Push this folder to GitHub.
2. In EdgeOne Pages, create a project from the repo (no build command, output directory = repo root).
3. Add env vars: `GEMINI_API_KEY` (required), `GEMINI_MODEL` (optional, default `gemini-2.5-flash`), `GEMINI_TTS_MODEL` (optional, default `gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts`), `GEMINI_STT_MODEL` (optional, used by Cloud listening, defaults to `GEMINI_MODEL`).
4. Optional Google sign-in: create a Google OAuth **Web application** client ID, enable the Google Drive API, add your production origin (and any local test origin) as an authorized JavaScript origin, then put the client ID in the `google-client-id` meta tag near the top of `index.html`. No client secret is needed for this browser token flow.
5. Redeploy. Open the site on your phone over HTTPS and use "Add to Home Screen" for the offline app.

## What's inside
- **New job wizard:** full-screen setup for vehicle, one or more services, condition, issues, optional photos, client and ETA. Runs on first launch and from Job > New job. Cancel leaves the current job untouched.
- **Job (home):** vehicle card with progress ring, multi-service picker (full exterior, paint correction, interior detail, interior deep clean, trim restoration, headlight restoration, maintenance wash, engine bay), combined checklist, progress tracker, site weather, shortcut tiles.
- **Ask:** streaming chat with typing effect and a stop button, voice input, photo/video attach, quick chips. Job context goes with every message.
- **Tools:** Mix (dilution calculator, presets), Timers (standard or large digits), Depth (multi-spot paint depth grid).
- **Kit:** chemicals with mix ratios, tools and equipment. Chemical entries can jump to the calculator.
- **Log:** inspection photos, notes, client text templates.
- **Account:** optional Google sign-in that backs up job data, kit, paint readings and photos to Google Drive app data, with restore, sync and delete controls in Settings.
- **Legal:** Privacy Policy (`privacy.html`) and Terms of Service (`terms.html`), linked from Settings and onboarding.
- **Audio:** Gemini voices with an automatic fallback to the best voice on the device. Pick them in Settings.

## Site version and update wall
The current version is shown in Settings and beside the Lustre title when space allows. To ship an update, change `SITE_VERSION` near the top of the script in `index.html`, then add or edit the matching entry in `SITE_UPDATES` (newest first). The update wall opens automatically for returning users when the version changes, and is always available from Settings > What’s new. Bump the cache name in `sw.js` whenever you change the app shell.

## Google sign-in and Drive backup
The app works fully without an account. With a Google OAuth Web Client ID configured, Settings shows **Sign in with Google**. After consent, Lustre writes two JSON files to the hidden `appDataFolder` in the user's own Google Drive:

- `lustre-job.json` - current job, settings, kit, timers, notes and paint-depth readings.
- `lustre-photos.json` - job inspection photos.

Signing in on another device offers to restore that backup. While signed in, changes sync automatically after a short debounce. The access token stays in memory; the app stores only the Google profile and Drive file IDs in local storage. **Delete cloud backup** removes both Drive files without touching local data. Lustre cannot see the rest of the user's Drive because it only requests `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.appdata`.

The client ID is public and lives in:

```html
<meta name="google-client-id" content="YOUR_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com">
```

Configure the OAuth consent screen, add the production origin under **Authorized JavaScript origins**, and add test users while the app is in testing. No client secret is required. Google may require OAuth verification before external users can grant the `drive.appdata` scope, so plan for the consent-screen review before a public launch.

## Privacy and terms
`privacy.html` and `terms.html` are styled standalone pages linked from Settings, the Google account panel and first-run onboarding. They contain visible placeholders for the operator name, contact email and governing region. Replace those before publishing, and have the final text reviewed for your jurisdiction. The privacy policy describes local storage, Google Drive app data, Gemini/EdgeOne processing, Open-Meteo, notifications and the Google API Limited Use disclosure.

## Multiple services
Select one or more services during setup or from the Job tab. Lustre merges shared stages (for example Wash or Correct) into one checklist and orders the remaining stages for the job. The package label, progress tracker, client texts and AI context all use the full service list.

## Paint depth
Each of the nine standard panels (`hood`, `roof`, `trunk`, `door_driver`, `door_passenger`, `fender_fl`, `fender_fr`, `quarter_rl`, `quarter_rr`) keeps any number of readings for the job in the IndexedDB store `paint_depth_logs` (keyPath `jobId`). Readings are always stored in µm and shown in µm or mils, so switching units never changes the numbers. Min, max, average and status are recomputed on every save. Status uses the lowest spot: safe above 110 µm, caution 85–110 µm, danger below 85 µm (flashing red on the car map).

## Alerts and timers
- Headphone alerts use native system notifications through the service worker. Enable them in Settings; the OS decides whether the sound routes to connected headphones.
- Larger timers make the digits glanceable from the bench.
- Timers and job alerts run while Lustre is open. Background delivery while the app is closed needs a push backend.
- The service worker and `/api/push/subscribe` hook are in place, but `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` in `index.html` is empty. Add a VAPID public key and a sender endpoint to enable server push.

## Hey Lustre
Two listening engines (Settings > Listening engine):
- **Browser** uses the browser's speech recognition. Free and private, but iPhone Home Screen apps do not have it at all, and Safari only allows it with Dictation turned on and a tap to start.
- **Cloud** keeps the microphone open, detects speech locally, and sends only short clips that contain speech to `/api/stt` (Gemini) to listen for “Hey Lustre”. It needs the screen on, so Lustre requests a screen wake lock. It is limited to 12 clips a minute and pauses while Lustre is talking. Turn it on from Settings, or accept the prompt that appears when Browser is unavailable.

The wake phrase is matched loosely because phones mishear “Lustre” (luster, lester, lusta, lust er). Say “Hey Lustre” followed by a command, or say it alone and then the command. **Settings > Check voice** tests the microphone and speech recognition separately and tells you which one is blocked.

Commands run locally first and fall back to the Gemini chat. Examples:
- Job: “set vehicle to 2022 BMW M3”, “set client to Sam”, “set ETA to 3 PM”, “add note that trim needs dressing”, “add paint correction”, “next step”, “what’s next”.
- Timers: “start a 5 minute dwell timer”, “cancel the cure timer”, “how much time is left”, “large timers on”.
- Depth and mix: “log 120 microns on the hood”, “add 4.5 mils to the driver’s door”, “paint depth status”, “switch depth to mils”, “calculate 1 to 10 for a 32 ounce bottle”.
- App: “open timers”, “open kit”, “show checklist”, “what’s the weather”, “audio off”, “what’s new”, “help”.

## iOS home screen
`apple-touch-icon.png` (180 px), `icon-192.png`, `icon-512.png` and `icon-maskable-512.png` are generated from the Lustre mark. In Safari, tap Share > Add to Home Screen to use it as the app icon.

## Offline
Everything except chat, Gemini voice, live weather, Google sign-in/sync and wake-word speech recognition works offline. Data lives on the device (localStorage and IndexedDB). If Google sign-in is enabled, a copy can also live in the user's Google Drive app data folder.

## Media in chat
Photos are resized in the browser. Videos are reduced to 8 frames to stay under edge payload limits.
*/